# Project rules (full detail in AGENTS.md at the repo root)

@AGENTS.md

## Data safety — never without asking

Never delete, truncate, drop, move, reset, reseed, or recreate a database.
Both `data/newsixity.db` (dev) and
`~/Library/Application Support/Newsixity/newsixity.db` (packaged macOS app)
hold real user data and cannot be regenerated from the repo.

A "table or column doesn't exist" error is a **migration bug to fix** (see
`_add_column_if_missing` in `backend/app/db/init_db.py`), never grounds for
touching the database file.

Point disposable runs at a temp DB instead:
`NEWSIXITY_DB_PATH=/tmp/scratch.db backend/.venv/bin/python -m pytest`

## Verify fixes

Reproduce with a failing test first, confirm it fails for the right reason,
fix it, then show the full suite green:
`cd backend && .venv/bin/python -m pytest -q` and
`npx tsc --noEmit && npx eslint src && npm run build`.

## Silent failure is the common defect here

Most shipped bugs are swallowed errors rendering empty UI. `apiError.ts` only
reads `detail`; non-OK responses are often discarded. Surface the real error
instead of adding a fallback.